    "title": "Teen Arrested for Burglary of Atascocita Business, $5,000 in Merchandise Stolen - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Amalia Weigandt ,\n18 hours ago Katreyvian Gonzalez ATASCOCITA, TX – On Saturday, November 8, 2025, deputies with Constable Mark Herman’s Office responded to a reported burglary at a business in the 20600 block of West Lake Houston Parkway in Atascocita. Upon arrival, deputies observed the front door glass had been shattered by a rock.\nInvestigators determined that 17-year-old Katreyvian Gonzalez, along with two unidentified accomplices, had forcibly entered the business and stolen approximately $5,000 worth of merchandise.\nWhile deputies were searching the area, a suspicious person call led them to locate Gonzalez hiding in a backyard behind the business. Gonzalez was arrested and booked into the Harris County Jail, charged with Burglary of a Building. His bond was set at $3,000 out of the 338th District Court.\nThe investigation remains ongoing as authorities continue efforts to identify and apprehend the other individuals involved.\nThe post first appeared on .\n4",
